      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(During Aseres Yemei Teshuvah say:)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "rubric"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(On fast days say:)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "rubric"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "(The following nine are said responsively—first by the chazzan:)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "rubric"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The following five are said during Aseres Yemei Teshuvah:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of good life. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ כָּתְבֵנוּ בְּסֵפֶר חַיִּים טוֹבִים:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of those who will see the geulah and be saved. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ כָּתְבֵנוּ בְּסֵפֶר גְּאֻלָּה וִישׁוּעָה:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of those who will be able earn a living and have their material needs. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ כָּתְבֵנוּ בְּסֵפֶר פַּרְנָסָה וְכַלְכָּלָה:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of merits. (See Instant Insight on the next page.) אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ כָּתְבֵנוּ בְּסֵפֶר זְכִיּוֹת:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, write us in the book of those who will be pardoned and forgiven. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ כָּתְבֵנוּ בְּסֵפֶר סְלִיחָה וּמְחִילָה:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "rubric"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "The following five are said on fast days:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us that we should have a life that is good. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ זָכְרֵנוּ לְחַיִּים טוֹבִים:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us and bring the geulah and save us. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ זָכְרֵנוּ לִגְאֻלָּה וִישׁוּעָה:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us and ensure we earn a living and have our material needs. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ זָכְרֵנוּ לְפַרְנָסָה וְכַלְכָּלָה:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us for merits. (See Instant Insight on the next page.) אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ זָכְרֵנוּ לִזְכִיּוֹת:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "callout",
      "tags": [
        "conditional"
      ],
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Our Father, our King, remember us and pardon and forgive us. אָבִינוּ מַלְכֵּנוּ זָכְרֵנוּ לִסְלִיחָה וּמְחִילָה:"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "instant_insight",
      "body": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "Instant Insight: Regarding the \"book of merits\" or remembering us \"for merits\": Either one has merits or they do not! If they do, they are in the book; and if not, what is Hashem supposed to do? What does this mean? The idea here is that Hashem could arrange your life so that it's easy for you to pick up merits and good deeds (someone in front of you drops something and you pick it up!) or the opposite—you simply do not have easy opportunities to do good deeds. We are asking Hashem to please remember us and write us in the book of those who will have many opportunities to do mitzvos!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}